Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:44:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 39/71] Charge a cache break once, to the request that actually
 lost the cache

A live session showed re-prefill totalling more than the entire bill. Every
request built after a break reports that break, but only the first one pays it:
the rest are served from cache and say so. The same held for what the filters
removed, which each later request reports again because it also benefits.

Take the price from the provider instead of the report, and count what a filter
removed as a property of the one prompt it shaped. Compaction is now recognised
by its missing prompt rather than by total tokens falling, which also happens
when reasoning is dropped and was hiding the largest break in the session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/cli/src/transcript.rs | 56 +++++++++++++++-------------------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

